{"kind":"artifact","text":"The MCP adapter refuses a durable act through an untrustworthy resident advertisement, naming which of the six classes it is, while a read still answers from the verified local fold. Exact clean pushed head 4990f83bb52a0052fdb1946fdd0edbced5c346e9 on request/mcp-advert-durable-refusal; local and origin identical by commit SHA and tree hash ba161928, checkout clean, main untouched at 02558e8d. Under planner's 7e55339e and my promise 85c73730.\n\nTHE DEFECT. room.endpoint() collapsed three answers into two, so every one of the six untrustworthy classes reached submit() as \"no resident\" and fell through to a local fold — a durable act folded locally because of a file any local process can write. gs already refuses in that situation; this surface did not.\n\nTHE REPAIR, AND WHY CONDITION (3) WAS NOT NEEDED. resolveEndpoint() reports three outcomes: an address, absence, or untrusted with the reason. endpoint() is now a thin wrapper discarding the reason, so all seven read and presence call sites are unchanged in behaviour. submit() calls resolveEndpoint() and refuses on error. The obstacle the old comment claimed — that there was no channel to refuse a whole attachment — was real but beside the point: nothing requires refusing the attachment. submit() is the single chokepoint for every durable act, so an error there refuses one call while the room, its lease and its session survive.\n\nORDERING, WHICH I VERIFIED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. In submit(), resolveEndpoint() is called at line 1116 and workspace.Actor() at 1120, so the refusal happens before the signing key is read. That is the property gs already documents for itself, and it now holds on both surfaces.\n\nTHE WORDING IS SHARED RATHER THAN REIMPLEMENTED. internal/residentclient now owns the two sentences: UntrustedAdvertisement for the five record-level classes and UnusableAdvertisedURL for the sixth, the address that is not a bare http loopback. cmd/gs was rewired through them and its output is byte-identical — I read the diff and the format strings are preserved verbatim, with the sentence moved inside the wrapper. Only the way-out clause differs between surfaces, and it must: --server is retired and ignored on this binary, so offering it here would be false. The adapter says nothing was appended and points at repairing the record or folding locally with gs.\n\nALL SIX CLASSES ARE COVERED, AND THE REASON IS NOT COMPLETENESS FOR ITS OWN SAKE. Five arrive through app.ResidentAdvertisement's Reason; the sixth passes that check and is caught one step later by ValidateURL, through the other sentence. Testing only the first group would leave the second sentence unexercised.\n\nMUTATION, RUN BY ME. Replacing submit()'s resolution with the treat-as-absent form fails all six subtests of TestUntrustedAdvertisementRefusesADurableAct with \"a durable act was accepted while the advertisement could not be trusted\" at untrusted_advertisement_test.go:121. The read test stayed green throughout, which is the point of the split. Restored; git status empty and the tree hash unchanged at ba161928.\n\nONE SIMPLIFICATION DELIBERATELY LEFT. resolveEndpoint still re-runs ValidateURL on a cached baseURL each call. That branch is reachable only because a test constructs a room with an unvalidated baseURL directly; in production baseURL only ever holds ValidateURL's own idempotent output. Removing it would shrink the function but would be a genuine read-path change, and this row is about the write path.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD, from a run I watched exit rather than taken from the agent that wrote the code. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 35 packages, zero failures and zero cached, with cmd/gitseq-mcp ok at 130.282s; gofmt -l . empty; go build ./... and go vet ./... exit 0 with no output; git diff --check exit 0. No ui/ change, so make ui was not run and I am not claiming it.","body":{"commit":"4990f83bb52a0052fdb1946fdd0edbced5c346e9","path":"cmd/gitseq-mcp"}}